      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T19:01:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would there be any benefit in using the config flag (`CONFIG_PRINTF_DISABLE_32BIT_LONG_WORKAROUND`) here then add a separate test to ensure that our FPMCU boards set the flag?\n\nIf someone looks at `printf` code in the future it might not be obvious why the implementation uses a conditional logic based on `CONFIG_PRINTF_DISABLE_32BIT_LONG_WORKAROUND` while the tests use board names.\n\nOr maybe my suggestions is only making things more complicated 😊",
      "parentUuid": "256b9ab8_f09de30f",
